<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saraychik</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saraishyq</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saraychik was a medieval town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Ural River</a> in western Kazakhstan, upstream from modern Atyrau. It was a trading station of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> on the route from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>, was sacked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> in 1395, and later became the seat of the Nogai Horde, whose rulers were buried there. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> destroyed it in 1580.</p></div>
